WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.006
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.276 --> 00:09.180
With one month until the Hakone Ekiden, Dainichi TV's crew,

3
00:09.747 --> 00:12.484
led by chief producer Ryo Tokushige,

4
00:12.550 --> 00:14.919
works feverishly on preparations.

5
00:14.986 --> 00:18.123
But Programming Bureau Chief Kuroishi,

6
00:18.189 --> 00:20.658
obsessed with ratings, pressures them

7
00:20.725 --> 00:23.228
to turn the broadcast into more of a variety show.

8
00:23.294 --> 00:26.898
Our job as a TV station is to show their race as it truly is.

9
00:26.965 --> 00:29.701
Exactly as it happens. That's all.

10
00:30.568 --> 00:35.240
Meanwhile, at Meisei Gakuin University, which failed to qualify,

11
00:35.306 --> 00:39.310
Coach Moroya appoints Masato Kai, a trading company employee, as head coach.

12
00:39.377 --> 00:44.482
You're going to Hakone, right? With the Student United Team.

13
00:45.316 --> 00:49.354
Hayato joins the Student United Team, made up of runners

14
00:49.420 --> 00:50.955
whose schools failed to qualify.

15
00:51.022 --> 00:51.656
‎STUDENT UNITED TEAM ‎A MAKESHIFT TEAM OF RUNNERS

16
00:51.723 --> 00:55.260
Kai also takes charge of the Student United Team.

17
00:55.760 --> 00:58.496
My goal is a top-three finish at the Hakone Ekiden.

18
00:58.563 --> 01:00.532
Hakone would be far better off.

19
01:01.132 --> 01:05.570
But the members clash fiercely over if teams like that were abolished.

20
01:05.637 --> 01:09.040
The unconventional policies of Kai, who has no coaching experience.

21
01:09.107 --> 01:11.743
Mr. Kitano says he wants to resign as coach.

22
01:11.809 --> 01:13.011
You quit too.

23
01:15.747 --> 01:19.918
Those aiming for Hakone fight their way back from adversity.

24
01:26.824 --> 01:29.694
For the past three years, Dainichi TV has failed

25
01:30.395 --> 01:32.330
to win the ratings triple crown.

26
01:32.397 --> 01:34.098
DAINICHI TV

27
01:34.165 --> 01:36.301
But this year,

28
01:37.001 --> 01:39.871
if half our programs beat last year's ratings…

29
01:39.938 --> 01:40.772
DAINICHI TV PROGRAMMING BUREAU CHIEF-TAKESHI KUROISHI

30
01:40.838 --> 01:44.008
…we can take the crown back from Kanto TV.

31
01:44.742 --> 01:47.445
What matters now is the year-end and New Year's ratings.

32
01:47.512 --> 01:48.479
DAINICHI TV MANAGING DIRECTOR MASAOMI KASHIWAGI

33
01:48.546 --> 01:49.881
And the centerpiece of New Year's is?

34
01:50.648 --> 01:51.516
It's Hakone.

35
01:51.583 --> 01:52.417
SPORTS BUREAU CHIEF YOSHIO KITAMURA

36
01:52.483 --> 01:53.885
As Dainichi TV's flagship program,

37
01:53.952 --> 01:57.355
if its ratings don't beat last year's,

38
01:58.122 --> 02:02.227
our chances of reclaiming the Triple Crown remain uncertain.

39
02:03.161 --> 02:04.796
Kuroishi is right.

40
02:04.862 --> 02:07.565
The Hakone Ekiden could determine our company's future.

41
02:08.933 --> 02:10.468
-Bureau Chief Kitamura. -Yes.

42
02:12.403 --> 02:13.871
Are preparations going smoothly?

43
02:13.938 --> 02:15.039
Everyone in

44
02:15.106 --> 02:17.508
the Sports Department is giving everything we have for race day.

45
02:18.176 --> 02:19.110
I see.

46
02:20.011 --> 02:21.346
I'm counting on you.

47
02:21.412 --> 02:23.715
We'll keep doing our utmost.

48
02:25.650 --> 02:29.988
He's creating a plan to beat last year's ratings.

49
02:30.054 --> 02:33.191
I could see it in Kuroishi's eyes.

50
02:33.258 --> 02:34.092
CHIEF PRODUCER RYO TOKUSHIGE

51
02:34.158 --> 02:36.027
Why are you so scared?

52
02:36.094 --> 02:39.130
Kuroishi's pressure is nothing new.

53
02:39.197 --> 02:42.734
True, but he's on a roll right now.

54
02:44.836 --> 02:47.372
That viewer-participation drama, The Ending Is Up to You?

55
02:47.438 --> 02:48.506
That's the one.

56
02:48.573 --> 02:51.909
It was a drama mixed with variety elements, with viewers taking part.

57
02:51.976 --> 02:54.212
Kuroishi got that show approved with one word.

58
02:54.279 --> 02:55.546
The one where viewers voted

59
02:55.613 --> 02:57.615
online to choose the ending?

60
02:57.682 --> 02:58.816
Exactly. And that's not all.

61
02:59.550 --> 03:02.453
He also ran drama and variety slots back-to-back.

62
03:02.520 --> 03:05.857
Everything Kuroishi tries seems to work.

63
03:05.923 --> 03:06.958
So what?

64
03:07.025 --> 03:09.027
We should have viewers

65
03:09.093 --> 03:11.629
-vote online and predict the standings? -Oh.

66
03:11.696 --> 03:12.697
Something like that.

67
03:12.764 --> 03:14.699
Are you serious?

68
03:14.766 --> 03:16.801
Don't be ridiculous.

69
03:16.868 --> 03:20.071
We've always said the runners are the stars. We're not changing that.

70
03:20.138 --> 03:22.140
I know.

71
03:22.206 --> 03:23.841
Despite that,

72
03:24.742 --> 03:27.078
making a good show is the minimum.

73
03:27.145 --> 03:29.580
We also have to beat last year's ratings.

74
03:30.848 --> 03:34.252
Finding a way to do that is part of your job, right?

75
03:35.553 --> 03:37.088
That's true, but…

76
03:37.155 --> 03:38.289
Right?

77
03:38.356 --> 03:41.326
I'm talking about the presentation. The way we show it?

78
03:41.392 --> 03:43.761
We need to make an effort

79
03:44.595 --> 03:45.596
to do something different.

80
03:45.663 --> 03:47.532
Like what?

81
03:47.598 --> 03:49.867
So… you want us to dress it up?

82
03:49.934 --> 03:52.403
Not dress it up! Be creative!

83
03:53.571 --> 03:55.707
You know the rumor, right?

84
03:57.775 --> 03:59.977
About the General Production Bureau?

85
04:00.044 --> 04:01.913
Apparently it's finally being created next spring.

86
04:01.979 --> 04:05.883
Variety, drama, news and even

87
04:05.950 --> 04:07.852
sports will all fall under it.

88
04:08.686 --> 04:11.489
If he becomes the bureau chief,

89
04:12.190 --> 04:13.925
Hakone will be a mess.

90
04:14.492 --> 04:17.161
That's why we have to beat

91
04:17.228 --> 04:21.032
last year's numbers our way.

92
04:22.934 --> 04:24.202
Seriously?

93
04:24.268 --> 04:25.436
Yeah.

94
04:25.503 --> 04:28.940
When the General Production Bureau launches,

95
04:29.006 --> 04:30.708
I want you to run it as the bureau chief.

96
04:33.244 --> 04:34.178
Thank you.

97
04:34.245 --> 04:37.749
This absolutely has to succeed.

98
04:38.783 --> 04:41.185
I'm planning to give you personnel authority too.

99
04:41.252 --> 04:42.787
Do what you need to do.

100
04:42.854 --> 04:43.755
Yes.

101
04:45.656 --> 04:49.060
I'll do everything I can to meet your expectations.

102
04:58.970 --> 05:00.838
Hey. What's with her?

103
05:00.905 --> 05:01.739
BROADCAST DIRECTOR NATSUKI MIYAMOTO

104
05:01.806 --> 05:04.041
Apparently, The Other Hakone Ekiden moved her to tears.

105
05:04.108 --> 05:06.778
Good. I thought you made her cry.

106
05:07.578 --> 05:09.781
The water stations are amazing.

107
05:09.847 --> 05:10.748
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR CHIKA TOYAMA

108
05:10.815 --> 05:12.116
I never knew there was so much

109
05:12.183 --> 05:14.652
drama behind handing out water.

110
05:14.719 --> 05:17.088
I didn't know you had this emotional side.

111
05:17.155 --> 05:19.724
For example, have you heard this story?

112
05:19.791 --> 05:23.327
A team member who wasn't selected became a water station attendant.

113
05:23.394 --> 05:26.664
His parents traveled all the way to Hakone just

114
05:26.731 --> 05:28.966
to watch him run alongside a teammate for a few dozen meters.

115
05:29.033 --> 05:30.268
That makes you cry, right?

116
05:30.334 --> 05:31.702
Me?

117
05:32.303 --> 05:33.438
I guess.

118
05:33.504 --> 05:34.338
TWO WATER STATIONS SERVE LEGS 1 AND 6, STAFFED BY TEAMMATES OR RUNNER ASSOCIATES

119
05:34.405 --> 05:36.174
The water station helps

120
05:36.240 --> 05:38.776
the runners keep going.

121
05:39.510 --> 05:41.312
It's not just to help them hydrate.

122
05:41.379 --> 05:43.514
The words from the water station attendants

123
05:43.581 --> 05:46.250
can also give runners strength.

124
05:46.317 --> 05:48.486
Stories like this could really connect with viewers

125
05:48.553 --> 05:50.488
who don't know much about Hakone.

126
05:51.322 --> 05:53.424
Please feature the water stations more.

127
05:54.425 --> 05:57.428
Water stations? That might not be bad.

128
05:58.162 --> 05:59.330
Please.

129
05:59.397 --> 06:00.631
Look into how we could present it.

130
06:01.699 --> 06:03.301
Me?

131
06:03.367 --> 06:04.302
I'm counting on you.

132
06:07.872 --> 06:08.973
We are too.

133
06:12.944 --> 06:14.445
I shouldn't have said that.

134
06:14.512 --> 06:16.280
I'm not helping you.

135
06:16.347 --> 06:17.482
Come on.

136
06:17.548 --> 06:20.284
Mr. Tokushige, the art staff sent over the set proposal.

137
06:23.221 --> 06:25.022
HAKONE EKIDEN

138
06:25.089 --> 06:26.724
It's not bad,

139
06:26.791 --> 06:31.295
but it feels like it's missing something fresh.

140
06:31.829 --> 06:34.832
I told them not to change it too much. Was that wrong?

141
06:34.899 --> 06:37.668
Right, I know.

142
06:37.735 --> 06:39.837
But even so,

143
06:39.904 --> 06:43.741
don't you want one small new touch?

144
06:43.808 --> 06:45.343
What kind of touch?

145
06:45.409 --> 06:50.615
Something that says we tried something new this year.

146
06:51.616 --> 06:52.583
For example?

147
06:53.651 --> 06:55.987
I mean as an example…

148
06:56.554 --> 06:59.657
-So you want some kind of gimmick? -Not a gimmick.

149
07:00.525 --> 07:01.492
Creativity.

150
07:03.694 --> 07:05.997
This may sound strange, but…

151
07:07.598 --> 07:09.400
Mr. Tokushige, are you getting cold feet?

152
07:10.334 --> 07:11.769
You got to be joking.

153
07:12.537 --> 07:14.005
Of course not.

154
07:15.139 --> 07:16.474
-Mr. Tokushige. -Yeah?

155
07:16.541 --> 07:19.911
I heard Coach Kitano resigned as a coach of the Student United Team.

156
07:19.977 --> 07:21.812
Huh? Why?

157
07:22.346 --> 07:25.650
He says an inexperienced coach is pushing the runners around

158
07:25.716 --> 07:28.619
with a reckless goal. Apparently, it was in protest.

159
07:28.686 --> 07:29.987
About Coach Kai?

160
07:30.788 --> 07:33.357
I've wondered about it too.

161
07:33.424 --> 07:34.425
About what?

162
07:34.492 --> 07:36.294
About how Coach Kai was selected.

163
07:36.360 --> 07:38.296
He'd been away from track for years

164
07:38.362 --> 07:41.899
and had no coaching record. He must have known there would be

165
07:41.966 --> 07:44.402
criticism if he took over a traditional program like Meisei Gakuin.

166
07:45.636 --> 07:49.640
I've been wondering the same thing. I've called Coach Moroya over and over,

167
07:49.707 --> 07:51.142
but he won't pick up.

168
07:52.743 --> 07:54.679
Maybe I'll ask Mr. Yoneyama.

169
07:54.745 --> 07:56.013
Mr. Yoneyama?

170
07:57.114 --> 07:59.183
He's a devoted Meisei alumnus.

171
08:00.618 --> 08:02.553
He might know something.

172
08:03.120 --> 08:05.556
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

173
08:05.623 --> 08:06.557
HAKONE EKIDEN STUDENT UNITED TEAM COACH KITANO RESIGNS IN ANGER

174
08:07.992 --> 08:10.761
People are taking Coach Kitano's article at face value.

175
08:10.828 --> 08:13.197
The criticism of Coach Kai is growing.

176
08:13.831 --> 08:15.266
This isn't fair.

177
08:15.800 --> 08:16.801
Exactly.

178
08:16.867 --> 08:19.103
HAYATO AOBA KEITO YANO

179
08:20.171 --> 08:21.672
YUSUKE MAEJIMA

180
08:21.739 --> 08:23.641
I read Coach Kitano's article.

181
08:24.141 --> 08:27.278
Maybe Coach Kai has reached his limit.

182
08:27.878 --> 08:28.713
His limit?

183
08:29.280 --> 08:31.949
He's taking all this criticism and can't even defend himself.

184
08:33.050 --> 08:34.418
Defend himself?

185
08:35.219 --> 08:37.221
Coach Kai

186
08:37.288 --> 08:38.723
doesn't respond to critical articles

187
08:38.789 --> 08:42.393
-or abuse on social media. -It's not that he won't. Maybe he can't.

188
08:43.961 --> 08:48.265
Mr. Yoneyama said the alumni are making a huge issue of it too.

189
08:49.700 --> 08:52.536
But if the Student United Team gets results at Hakone…

190
08:54.338 --> 08:57.208
You seriously think it can finish in the top three?

191
08:58.609 --> 09:00.745
I think the individual runners have that potential.

192
09:00.811 --> 09:02.546
Coach Kai has done

193
09:02.613 --> 09:06.283
an excellent job coaching the Student United Team.

194
09:06.350 --> 09:07.218
What's left is teamwork.

195
09:07.284 --> 09:10.121
That's the exact opposite of what Coach Kitano says.

196
09:15.660 --> 09:16.494
Um…

197
09:18.129 --> 09:20.598
Coach Kitano mocked Coach Kai

198
09:20.665 --> 09:23.367
and then walked out on the team.

199
09:24.402 --> 09:26.404
He didn't consider the trouble he'd cause them.

200
09:26.971 --> 09:28.506
I don't think someone like

201
09:28.572 --> 09:30.775
that is fit to be a coach.

202
09:30.841 --> 09:32.276
What?

203
09:32.843 --> 09:34.612
Even you're taking his side now?

204
09:34.679 --> 09:37.314
This isn't about sides.

205
09:37.381 --> 09:38.883
Hey, Yusuke…

206
09:39.550 --> 09:41.619
I'm not asking you to support him.

207
09:42.920 --> 09:43.788
But

208
09:44.422 --> 09:47.825
can you stop believing every one-sided criticism and making a fuss over it?

209
09:50.594 --> 09:51.862
You're right.

210
09:53.364 --> 09:55.566
You're the captain of the Student United Team.

211
09:58.502 --> 10:01.372
Sorry for butting in.

212
10:03.541 --> 10:04.375
No.

213
10:05.309 --> 10:06.811
Thanks for worrying about us.

214
10:09.714 --> 10:13.050
I'm worried about Meisei's future.

215
10:14.218 --> 10:16.721
Coach Kai is our head coach too.

216
10:16.787 --> 10:19.890
If the Student United Team keeps getting him dragged online,

217
10:22.493 --> 10:23.961
how could I not be worried?

218
10:26.597 --> 10:27.932
I'll eat somewhere else.

219
10:31.669 --> 10:32.903
HAKONE EKIDEN STUDENT UNITED TEAM COACH KITANO RESIGNS IN ANGER

220
10:32.970 --> 10:34.672
AN UNQUALIFIED, INEXPERIENCED COACH IS LEADING THEM ASTRAY WITH RECKLESS GOALS

221
10:34.739 --> 10:37.408
Kitano really did it.

222
10:37.975 --> 10:40.678
I'm thinking of refusing to replace him. What do you think?

223
10:40.745 --> 10:43.714
Yeah, that's probably best.

224
10:43.781 --> 10:46.484
Too many cooks spoil the broth.

225
10:47.351 --> 10:49.286
More importantly, are you okay?

226
10:50.588 --> 10:53.724
I'll explain it to the runners at camp tomorrow.

227
10:54.258 --> 10:56.660
No, Kai. I mean you.

228
10:57.261 --> 10:58.095
Huh?

229
10:58.162 --> 11:01.232
With all this uproar, you must be hearing some cruel things.

230
11:04.168 --> 11:05.436
I'll be fine.

231
11:06.971 --> 11:10.674
So you still coach at Meisei sometimes?

232
11:10.741 --> 11:13.144
Yes, as a volunteer.

233
11:13.210 --> 11:14.044
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY ALUMNI KUYA YONEYAMA

234
11:14.979 --> 11:20.351
Why did Coach Moroya suddenly resign?

235
11:22.453 --> 11:26.624
Neither I nor the other alumni really know.

236
11:27.825 --> 11:32.563
Normally, a traditional program would consult

237
11:32.630 --> 11:35.933
the alumni carefully about a coaching appointment.

238
11:36.000 --> 11:38.469
At Meisei, Coach Moroya had the authority

239
11:38.536 --> 11:39.804
to choose his successor.

240
11:39.870 --> 11:42.973
But don't you think there are too many

241
11:43.040 --> 11:47.545
unknowns about Mr. Kai as a coach?

242
11:49.146 --> 11:50.314
Yes.

243
11:50.848 --> 11:53.350
Kai was three years behind me.

244
11:53.884 --> 11:58.355
He was a wonderful runner, but he has zero coaching experience.

245
11:58.889 --> 12:02.226
Putting someone like that in charge is a huge gamble.

246
12:02.293 --> 12:05.963
What do the other alumni think?

247
12:07.097 --> 12:10.334
Their dissatisfaction is close to boiling over.

248
12:11.101 --> 12:12.469
After Hakone,

249
12:12.536 --> 12:15.206
they're talking about reconsidering the appointment at the alumni meeting.

250
12:16.307 --> 12:18.242
I see.

251
12:20.644 --> 12:24.849
Actually, there's something else that bothers me.

252
12:27.084 --> 12:28.352
What do you mean?

253
12:29.386 --> 12:32.223
Kai used

254
12:32.289 --> 12:34.625
Tohto Chuo Bussan's social contribution program

255
12:35.426 --> 12:38.562
to accept the coaching job for one year.

256
12:38.629 --> 12:41.065
-One year? -Yes.

257
12:41.131 --> 12:44.034
He's only a temporary coach for one year.

258
12:44.935 --> 12:46.270
No way.

259
12:47.104 --> 12:50.774
Apparently the company encourages employees to use that program.

260
12:51.408 --> 12:55.479
There's a rumor that using it helps you get promoted.

261
12:55.546 --> 12:59.049
So he's doing this for a promotion?

262
13:04.521 --> 13:06.523
COACH MOROYA

263
13:12.596 --> 13:15.165
COACH MOROYA (HOME)

264
13:23.140 --> 13:24.909
Hello, Moroya residence.

265
13:24.975 --> 13:27.678
Hello. Sorry to call out of the blue.

266
13:27.745 --> 13:31.181
This is Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

267
13:31.248 --> 13:35.886
Oh, Mr. Tokushige! It's been a long time.

268
13:35.953 --> 13:37.187
It really has.

269
13:37.254 --> 13:39.390
How have you been doing?

270
13:39.456 --> 13:42.626
I'm managing. And you?

271
13:42.693 --> 13:43.794
I'm well.

272
13:43.861 --> 13:46.430
Are you covering Hakone again this year?

273
13:46.497 --> 13:47.531
Yes.

274
13:47.598 --> 13:51.669
Actually, that's partly why I'm calling. I've tried Coach Moroya's cell phone

275
13:51.735 --> 13:55.205
several times, but I haven't been able to reach him.

276
13:56.173 --> 13:57.675
I'm sorry.

277
13:59.543 --> 14:04.048
Actually, Mr. Tokushige, my husband…

278
14:06.016 --> 14:06.884
Huh?

279
14:08.218 --> 14:09.153
STUDENT UNITED TEAM PRACTICE DAY

280
14:09.219 --> 14:11.155
I'm sure you've all heard by now.

281
14:12.122 --> 14:15.025
Coach Kitano has left the Student United Team.

282
14:16.860 --> 14:20.564
The reason is a disagreement over how the team should be run.

283
14:20.631 --> 14:21.465
JO INOMATA, TAKUMI SAKIYAMA MAKOTO AMAGI

284
14:21.532 --> 14:24.969
I'm sorry this happened at a time

285
14:25.035 --> 14:26.837
when you should be focused.

286
14:28.238 --> 14:30.007
This is entirely my responsibility.

287
14:32.743 --> 14:33.744
I'm sorry.

288
14:37.481 --> 14:38.482
Um…

289
14:39.550 --> 14:41.952
Is Kota leaving too?

290
14:43.253 --> 14:45.055
I haven't heard anything from Kota yet.

291
14:45.122 --> 14:48.125
So he hasn't said he's quitting?

292
14:49.159 --> 14:50.027
But

293
14:50.561 --> 14:53.630
his university coach, the man he's followed all this time walked away.

294
14:55.866 --> 14:59.703
All we can do now is wait, but Kota will probably come.

295
15:23.027 --> 15:26.663
I'm thinking of quitting as coach of the Student United Team.

296
15:26.730 --> 15:27.598
KOTA MATSUKI

297
15:27.664 --> 15:28.532
Huh?

298
15:28.599 --> 15:29.900
Kai is the laughingstock

299
15:29.967 --> 15:32.036
of the track and field world now.

300
15:32.102 --> 15:33.337
‎COACH SEIWA INTERNATIONAL ‎STUDENT UNITED TEAM-KOICHI KITANO

301
15:35.005 --> 15:36.006
You quit too.

302
15:37.074 --> 15:40.644
I'll notify the Kanto Student Federation of my resignation tomorrow.

303
15:41.545 --> 15:42.880
You withdraw too.

304
15:44.648 --> 15:45.716
Understood?

305
15:53.390 --> 15:55.559
KEITO YANO

306
15:59.496 --> 16:01.432
HOSPICE CARE

307
16:02.800 --> 16:03.867
Yes?

308
16:06.737 --> 16:08.272
Excuse me.

309
16:09.073 --> 16:12.910
What? Why did you come all the way out here?

310
16:12.976 --> 16:13.877
I'm sorry.

311
16:14.611 --> 16:16.947
You wouldn't answer your phone.

312
16:17.948 --> 16:20.551
I'm doing a digital detox.

313
16:22.019 --> 16:25.789
I'm impressed you know such a trendy phrase.

314
16:26.390 --> 16:27.958
Of course I do.

315
16:28.025 --> 16:32.096
No matter how old I get, I've spent my life dealing with

316
16:32.162 --> 16:34.398
young college students.

317
16:34.465 --> 16:37.401
I've had to learn how to communicate with them.

318
16:38.735 --> 16:39.603
True.

319
16:40.370 --> 16:43.841
Coach Kitano quit the Student United Team?

320
16:44.374 --> 16:45.342
Yes.

321
16:46.243 --> 16:49.746
And recently, Coach Hirakawa of Tozai University

322
16:50.314 --> 16:52.616
criticized the Student United Team.

323
16:52.683 --> 16:56.820
Coach Kai is taking a lot of abuse online.

324
16:56.887 --> 16:59.089
So that's what's happening.

325
17:00.390 --> 17:05.696
There's something I've wanted to ask you.

326
17:06.396 --> 17:09.666
Why did you name Mr. Kai your successor?

327
17:11.068 --> 17:13.837
Someone like Yoneyama

328
17:13.904 --> 17:16.406
could probably have succeeded me.

329
17:17.241 --> 17:20.911
If all I wanted was to maintain the status quo, that would've been fine.

330
17:21.745 --> 17:22.946
But

331
17:23.480 --> 17:26.350
if I wanted to take Meisei

332
17:26.416 --> 17:29.219
to a new level,

333
17:29.286 --> 17:31.188
it had to be Masato Kai.

334
17:31.822 --> 17:33.924
I couldn't think of anyone else.

335
17:35.526 --> 17:36.960
You really trust him.

336
17:38.562 --> 17:42.199
Well, he's unproven as a coach.

337
17:43.133 --> 17:47.137
But he has imagination

338
17:47.204 --> 17:48.839
and flexibility.

339
17:48.906 --> 17:51.642
So you truly believe Coach Kai

340
17:51.708 --> 17:55.012
can build a new powerhouse.

341
17:55.746 --> 17:57.014
Is that so?

342
17:57.614 --> 17:59.650
Not just Meisei.

343
18:01.018 --> 18:02.553
The Student United Team too.

344
18:04.087 --> 18:06.056
Kai will change

345
18:06.924 --> 18:09.426
the history of Hakone.

346
18:13.597 --> 18:16.233
Kota didn't come after all.

347
18:16.900 --> 18:19.036
Maybe Coach Kitano stopped him.

348
18:19.102 --> 18:22.172
What does the coach have to do with it?

349
18:22.239 --> 18:23.941
We're the ones who run.

350
18:24.007 --> 18:26.376
-Yeah. -Right?

351
18:26.443 --> 18:27.678
Still, I don't know.

352
18:28.212 --> 18:29.646
I feel like I'm here

353
18:29.713 --> 18:31.915
because of Coach Onuma.

354
18:31.982 --> 18:33.984
So I understand Kota a little.

355
18:38.255 --> 18:41.124
Kota was fast at the time trial, wasn't he?

356
18:44.828 --> 18:46.763
He was amazing.

357
18:49.132 --> 18:52.502
If Kota leaves, we're in trouble.

358
18:54.504 --> 18:55.939
Then why don't you leave with him?

359
18:56.006 --> 18:57.507
You were hanging around with him.

360
18:59.676 --> 19:01.511
You're the one who was always with Kota.

361
19:01.578 --> 19:03.480
-You were! -Um…

362
19:04.548 --> 19:05.549
Let's stop.

363
19:06.083 --> 19:06.917
Yeah.

364
19:07.584 --> 19:09.486
This is when we need to pull together.

365
19:10.387 --> 19:13.590
But this is Coach Kai's fault in the first place.

366
19:13.657 --> 19:15.959
We know the coach isn't the bad guy.

367
19:16.727 --> 19:21.064
Actually, I once interviewed

368
19:21.131 --> 19:23.033
Mr. Kai when he was a runner.

369
19:23.100 --> 19:25.302
-I see. -Yes.

370
19:27.170 --> 19:31.975
That interview became a kind of a trauma for me as a TV journalist.

371
19:33.644 --> 19:35.012
A little wound

372
19:35.579 --> 19:37.214
I'd rather not remember.

373
19:38.715 --> 19:40.717
Did Kai say something to you?

374
19:43.520 --> 19:45.589
You could say that.

375
19:45.656 --> 19:46.490
20 YEARS AGO HAKONE EKIDEN-TOTSUKA RELAY POINT

376
19:46.556 --> 19:48.625
Congratulations on the fastest time on the second leg.

377
19:48.692 --> 19:49.526
Thank you.

378
19:49.593 --> 19:50.727
That was an incredible run.

379
19:50.794 --> 19:51.628
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY FIRST-YEAR MASATO KAI

380
19:51.695 --> 19:53.463
How did you feel when you crossed the goal first?

381
19:54.164 --> 19:55.232
It's "finish."

382
19:56.400 --> 19:58.835
In track and field, we say "finish," not "goal."

383
20:01.738 --> 20:04.975
-I'd just joined the Sports Department, -I'm sorry.

384
20:05.042 --> 20:06.977
but I hadn't done my homework.

385
20:07.044 --> 20:08.412
I mean…

386
20:09.313 --> 20:11.782
I was so embarrassed and ashamed.

387
20:12.516 --> 20:15.652
I've never been able to watch that interview again.

388
20:16.953 --> 20:18.989
That does sound like Kai.

389
20:19.556 --> 20:21.725
He probably couldn't forgive a TV reporter

390
20:21.792 --> 20:24.895
who couldn't report on track properly.

391
20:24.961 --> 20:25.796
Yes.

392
20:26.663 --> 20:30.300
Still, getting embarrassed by a college kid

393
20:30.367 --> 20:33.770
much younger than you must have hurt.

394
20:34.671 --> 20:35.539
Yes.

395
20:36.139 --> 20:39.109
People at the station teased me about it for a while.

396
20:39.843 --> 20:42.746
But that bitter experience is why

397
20:43.580 --> 20:46.550
I can now demand thorough research

398
20:47.617 --> 20:52.556
from my staff.

399
21:04.701 --> 21:08.071
Hello. I'm Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

400
21:08.972 --> 21:10.474
Why are you here?

401
21:12.175 --> 21:14.378
Coach Moroya's wife told me.

402
21:15.245 --> 21:16.179
I see.

403
21:17.114 --> 21:20.183
I finally understand why Coach Moroya

404
21:20.817 --> 21:21.952
resigned so suddenly.

405
21:23.153 --> 21:25.088
I'd appreciate it if you didn't report it.

406
21:25.155 --> 21:26.490
Of course.

407
21:26.556 --> 21:29.159
I'll respect the coach's wishes

408
21:29.226 --> 21:31.695
not to upset the runners.

409
21:32.329 --> 21:33.163
Please.

410
21:33.964 --> 21:37.100
By the way, the runners seem distracted

411
21:37.167 --> 21:40.404
by something else right now.

412
21:40.470 --> 21:42.038
Will they be okay?

413
21:42.873 --> 21:44.641
Yes. Don't worry.

414
21:46.143 --> 21:49.112
This isn't an interview.

415
21:49.679 --> 21:53.650
I'd like to ask you something personally.

416
21:55.252 --> 21:56.720
Why did you

417
21:57.287 --> 22:00.323
agree to succeed Coach Moroya?

418
22:02.359 --> 22:04.494
I don't think I need to answer that.

419
22:08.365 --> 22:11.935
I respect Coach Moroya.

420
22:12.436 --> 22:16.706
I want to believe he was right

421
22:16.773 --> 22:18.642
to entrust everything to you.

422
22:19.609 --> 22:22.312
But I still can't understand

423
22:22.379 --> 22:28.585
what kind of man Masato Kai is.

424
22:30.220 --> 22:33.123
I think you'll understand if you watch the race.

425
22:33.890 --> 22:34.724
Huh?

426
22:34.791 --> 22:39.396
The result will prove Coach Moroya made the right choice.

427
22:42.866 --> 22:43.834
Excuse me.

428
22:47.804 --> 22:50.340
That was way too cool.

429
22:53.977 --> 22:56.112
I heard from Tokushige.

430
22:57.047 --> 23:01.585
You didn't have to come see me when you've got so much going on.

431
23:05.489 --> 23:09.192
I came to apologize today.

432
23:10.393 --> 23:13.029
You have nothing to apologize to me for.

433
23:13.997 --> 23:17.133
Everything that happened is due to my shortcomings.

434
23:20.270 --> 23:23.373
You still have a lot of enemies.

435
23:24.908 --> 23:27.210
The nail that sticks out gets hammered down.

436
23:27.711 --> 23:29.913
I don't care what people say about me.

437
23:30.514 --> 23:31.348
But

438
23:32.048 --> 23:34.684
I never wanted the runners to suffer because of it.

439
23:35.285 --> 23:36.953
I feel terrible about that.

440
23:37.954 --> 23:40.290
You knew what you were getting into?

441
23:42.392 --> 23:46.563
I couldn't have accepted a responsibility this big without being prepared.

442
23:49.199 --> 23:50.100
I see.

443
23:50.600 --> 23:51.835
Yes.

444
23:55.872 --> 23:59.576
I was talking with Tokushige earlier.

445
24:01.344 --> 24:04.080
It made me wonder again.

446
24:05.615 --> 24:09.452
Why did you accept

447
24:09.519 --> 24:13.990
my request? He wanted to know the reason too.

448
24:15.458 --> 24:17.827
Now you're asking?

449
24:19.162 --> 24:21.865
Yeah. I'm asking now.

450
24:22.933 --> 24:24.701
There are several reasons.

451
24:25.335 --> 24:28.438
One is something you taught me.

452
24:31.141 --> 24:32.142
Me?

453
24:33.109 --> 24:34.077
Yes.

454
24:35.645 --> 24:37.314
A crucial second shot.

455
24:37.380 --> 24:40.750
Ogiso has practiced shots from this distance over and over.

456
24:40.817 --> 24:42.018
This one's going to get close!

457
24:43.954 --> 24:44.788
What a shot!

458
24:44.854 --> 24:47.257
-Mr. Karashima sure is something else. -Past the pin! A birdie chance!

459
24:47.324 --> 24:49.259
For better or worse,

460
24:49.326 --> 24:51.328
Dainichi Golf coverage is synonymous with Karashima.

461
24:51.394 --> 24:53.096
He's a pain, though.

462
24:53.163 --> 24:54.497
We're in a meeting.

463
24:54.564 --> 24:56.533
Hey! You don't have to turn it off!

464
24:56.600 --> 24:58.168
We'll still do the meeting.

465
24:58.234 --> 25:00.270
Then I'll mute it.

466
25:00.337 --> 25:01.571
Good morning.

467
25:01.638 --> 25:03.006
-Good morning. -Good morning.

468
25:06.476 --> 25:07.577
THE NEW DESIGN-MIYAMOTO

469
25:07.644 --> 25:10.380
Huh? Mr. Tokushige never came back?

470
25:10.447 --> 25:12.415
Maybe it really can't be done.

471
25:12.482 --> 25:15.051
The crowd noise is huge.

472
25:15.118 --> 25:17.187
You're here on a Sunday? That's rare.

473
25:17.253 --> 25:20.290
I was watching old footage until late last night,

474
25:20.357 --> 25:22.092
and something about the voices bothered me.

475
25:22.158 --> 25:23.426
-The voices? -Yes.

476
25:23.493 --> 25:24.761
The voices at the water station.

477
25:25.328 --> 25:27.998
Those two runners have been classmates since high school.

478
25:28.064 --> 25:30.900
Kawaguchi was running Hakone for the first time.

479
25:30.967 --> 25:34.304
Suzuki was injured and left off the team, so he was assigned to the water station.

480
25:34.371 --> 25:37.173
They were both seniors, and it was their last Hakone.

481
25:37.240 --> 25:38.842
Oh, that was last year.

482
25:38.908 --> 25:39.843
Yes.

483
25:39.909 --> 25:41.978
Kawaguchi was nervous.

484
25:42.045 --> 25:46.082
Suzuki promised he'd make him laugh while running beside him with water.

485
25:46.149 --> 25:48.084
I saw it on The Other Hakone Ekiden.

486
25:48.151 --> 25:52.055
But I couldn't hear what Suzuki said to make him laugh.

487
25:52.122 --> 25:55.091
Getting clear audio in a crowd

488
25:55.158 --> 25:56.092
that loud is difficult.

489
25:56.159 --> 25:58.395
It feels like there should be some way.

490
25:58.461 --> 26:00.664
If there were, we'd already do it.

491
26:00.730 --> 26:02.932
I guess so…

492
26:03.733 --> 26:05.969
Oh! If he sinks this, he'll take the lead.

493
26:06.903 --> 26:09.673
Now, a birdie putt.

494
26:09.739 --> 26:10.940
OGISO

495
26:11.007 --> 26:12.308
Middle of the putt...

496
26:12.375 --> 26:14.477
-Yeah! -Yeah!

497
26:15.245 --> 26:16.646
-That sound just now! -Huh?

498
26:16.713 --> 26:18.081
How are they recording that?

499
26:18.148 --> 26:19.049
What?

500
26:19.115 --> 26:21.151
The sound of the ball dropping into the cup.

501
26:21.217 --> 26:22.952
It was incredibly clear, wasn't it?

502
26:23.019 --> 26:24.821
But you can't see a microphone on screen.

503
26:26.122 --> 26:27.424
Mr. Kuwana.

504
26:27.490 --> 26:29.459
Have we ever used that golf shotgun mic

505
26:29.526 --> 26:30.894
at a Hakone water station?

506
26:30.960 --> 26:34.264
-We're in a meeting. -Yeah…

507
26:35.131 --> 26:37.033
As far as I know, no.

508
26:37.100 --> 26:39.302
Then could one of those mics pick up

509
26:39.369 --> 26:40.870
a runner's voice during the race?

510
26:40.937 --> 26:43.606
But Hakone is different…

511
26:44.307 --> 26:46.109
With those crowds, it would be difficult.

512
26:46.176 --> 26:48.278
But the chance isn't zero.

513
26:50.814 --> 26:53.316
Maybe not zero.

514
26:54.284 --> 26:55.485
Can we test it?

515
26:55.552 --> 26:57.420
-I said we're in a meeting! -Hey!

516
26:57.487 --> 26:58.988
Help her get the equipment.

517
26:59.055 --> 26:59.923
Yes.

518
27:00.590 --> 27:01.991
-Thank you. -Thank you.

519
27:04.794 --> 27:06.863
Guys! Look!

520
27:07.497 --> 27:08.665
Did you see this?

521
27:10.133 --> 27:11.668
This is awful.

522
27:11.735 --> 27:12.569
DO WE EVEN NEED A STUDENT UNITED TEAM? PROBABLY DON'T NEED THEM

523
27:12.635 --> 27:13.770
Here's another one.

524
27:16.539 --> 27:19.342
"We don't need the Student United Team."

525
27:19.876 --> 27:21.811
"Who'd be moved by rivals

526
27:21.878 --> 27:24.681
from different schools passing a sash to each other?"

527
27:24.748 --> 27:25.949
That's what it says.

528
27:26.015 --> 27:27.083
That's messed up.

529
27:27.150 --> 27:29.085
"People still see the Student United Team

530
27:29.152 --> 27:31.321
as runners pulling in different directions…"

531
27:31.387 --> 27:33.456
The criticism on social media is really catching fire.

532
27:33.523 --> 27:34.924
-Huh? -Who said that?

533
27:34.991 --> 27:37.327
-That pisses me off! -That's awful, isn't it?

534
27:37.393 --> 27:38.661
I see.

535
27:39.796 --> 27:40.930
Yes.

536
27:40.997 --> 27:45.068
We were finally starting to come together.

537
27:45.135 --> 27:47.403
But everyone thinks differently,

538
27:47.937 --> 27:49.672
and we're losing focus.

539
27:50.774 --> 27:54.744
As ฉaptain, what should I say to them?

540
27:57.747 --> 27:58.648
Hayato.

541
27:59.349 --> 28:00.450
Yes?

542
28:01.417 --> 28:03.820
Don't forget the most important thing.

543
28:06.222 --> 28:08.958
Our goal of finishing in the top three?

544
28:10.794 --> 28:12.061
Then…

545
28:15.832 --> 28:18.501
You and Mr. Kai joined the company at the same time, right?

546
28:19.068 --> 28:20.003
Yes.

547
28:20.637 --> 28:24.941
Mr. Kai still technically has a position at the company, doesn't he?

548
28:25.008 --> 28:26.009
KAI'S COLLEAGUE AT TOHTO CHUO BUSSAN REIJI WAKUDA

549
28:26.075 --> 28:29.412
He's using the one-year social contribution program.

550
28:30.814 --> 28:34.717
So he'll coach for one year

551
28:34.784 --> 28:38.087
and then return to the company?

552
28:39.355 --> 28:40.190
No.

553
28:41.658 --> 28:43.359
Knowing Kai,

554
28:44.761 --> 28:46.763
I think he accepted the coaching job

555
28:47.297 --> 28:48.932
intending never to return.

556
28:49.566 --> 28:52.735
Then why use the program

557
28:52.802 --> 28:54.504
instead of resigning?

558
28:56.039 --> 28:57.774
He never told me,

559
28:59.342 --> 29:03.880
but I think it was so he wouldn't receive coaching pay

560
29:03.947 --> 29:05.849
from the university for one year.

561
29:08.151 --> 29:11.988
You mean Mr. Kai wanted his coaching pay

562
29:12.522 --> 29:14.524
to go to the team instead?

563
29:16.059 --> 29:19.062
That's probably what he intended.

564
29:19.829 --> 29:20.830
But

565
29:20.897 --> 29:24.367
what about his work at the company?

566
29:25.168 --> 29:28.938
I heard he had a career

567
29:29.005 --> 29:30.240
that took him around the world.

568
29:33.009 --> 29:33.877
Yes.

569
29:35.912 --> 29:36.746
He did.

570
29:38.214 --> 29:39.282
He did?

571
29:42.352 --> 29:46.089
Back then, Kai poured even more passion

572
29:46.155 --> 29:48.391
into his work than anyone else.

573
29:48.458 --> 29:51.828
What kind of work did he do?

574
29:53.396 --> 29:54.998
He was in the steel division's

575
29:55.064 --> 29:57.467
prestigious overseas department.

576
29:57.533 --> 30:00.069
He led several successful M&amp;A deals

577
30:00.136 --> 30:01.971
with an eye to future growth.

578
30:03.640 --> 30:05.975
His direct supervisor at the time

579
30:06.042 --> 30:07.477
was a department head named Harada.

580
30:07.543 --> 30:09.312
TOHTO CHUO BUSSAN

581
30:10.947 --> 30:12.782
You did it, Kai!

582
30:12.849 --> 30:15.685
I'm lucky to have such a dependable subordinate.

583
30:16.552 --> 30:17.787
Thank you.

584
30:21.557 --> 30:24.694
Harada favored Kai,

585
30:25.361 --> 30:27.263
and Kai respected him.

586
30:28.631 --> 30:29.766
Three years ago,

587
30:30.400 --> 30:34.337
Kai was put in charge of acquiring a mine in Brazil.

588
30:36.639 --> 30:39.275
At first, Kai refused.

589
30:39.342 --> 30:43.079
He said the long-term risk was too high.

590
30:44.113 --> 30:45.181
But…

591
30:46.049 --> 30:49.052
This is the president's project.

592
30:49.786 --> 30:50.653
However,

593
30:51.421 --> 30:54.357
there are serious concerns

594
30:54.424 --> 30:56.259
about this company's environmental record.

595
30:57.226 --> 30:59.295
Signing this deal is too risky.

596
30:59.362 --> 31:03.232
The president already gave his verbal approval.

597
31:06.336 --> 31:08.037
-Even so-- -Kai.

598
31:09.072 --> 31:12.742
That uncompromising integrity of yours

599
31:13.309 --> 31:16.612
is both a strength and a weakness.

600
31:18.748 --> 31:21.551
Sometimes you need to be flexible.

601
31:23.186 --> 31:25.288
-But-- -Don't worry.

602
31:25.855 --> 31:29.659
If anything happens, I'll take responsibility.

603
31:32.095 --> 31:37.734
I think Kai wanted to trust Harada.

604
31:39.736 --> 31:43.773
But later, environmental problems at the acquired company came to light.

605
31:43.840 --> 31:46.242
-Hey, this is bad. -Then they discovered

606
31:46.309 --> 31:48.211
a company-wide cover-up.

607
31:48.277 --> 31:50.780
-They went bankrupt. -The company

608
31:50.847 --> 31:53.016
was left with enormous losses.

609
31:53.082 --> 31:55.051
-We're going to get busy. -Yeah.

610
31:55.651 --> 31:56.619
Kai.

611
31:57.186 --> 32:00.523
I need you to wrap this matter up properly.

612
32:01.224 --> 32:02.125
Yes.

613
32:02.191 --> 32:04.827
That's your duty as project leader.

614
32:07.030 --> 32:09.699
When this project started two years ago,

615
32:10.433 --> 32:12.535
I warned you, didn't I?

616
32:13.202 --> 32:16.105
I understand you want to avoid responsibility, but…

617
32:19.275 --> 32:20.710
Wait.

618
32:21.711 --> 32:26.249
You told me that if anything happened, you would take responsibility.

619
32:27.784 --> 32:29.986
I don't remember saying that.

620
32:35.892 --> 32:40.163
Kai received a formal reprimand in the president's name.

621
32:42.532 --> 32:46.836
He was transferred to a department considered a dead end inside the company.

622
32:48.304 --> 32:49.672
After that,

623
32:51.874 --> 32:54.043
he clearly lost all his motivation.

624
32:56.913 --> 33:01.050
I never expected Mr. Harada to take responsibility.

625
33:02.552 --> 33:04.520
I knew he'd protect himself.

626
33:06.756 --> 33:08.391
At first, I believed in him.

627
33:09.158 --> 33:10.293
In my boss,

628
33:11.260 --> 33:12.995
and in the company's business.

629
33:14.630 --> 33:18.734
So I worked for the people I trusted and for the company.

630
33:20.570 --> 33:23.039
But as time passed,

631
33:24.407 --> 33:28.277
I realized the world I believed in wasn't that clean.

632
33:30.012 --> 33:32.381
It was a place where unreasonable things were allowed to happen.

633
33:35.251 --> 33:37.086
I knew that deep down, but I had shut my eyes to it.

634
33:41.824 --> 33:43.793
Wakuda, what do you work for?

635
33:49.532 --> 33:50.833
I don't know.

636
33:53.569 --> 33:54.804
I want to work…

637
33:58.875 --> 34:01.944
for something I can truly believe in.

638
34:04.981 --> 34:05.882
But now…

639
34:10.620 --> 34:13.589
Something I can truly believe in…

640
34:16.092 --> 34:16.926
Yes.

641
34:19.228 --> 34:20.196
Kai is once again

642
34:21.030 --> 34:24.934
devoting himself to something he believes in.

643
34:27.170 --> 34:29.005
That's why I want to support him.

644
34:34.210 --> 34:35.177
TOHTO CHUO BUSSAN SUCCEEDED IN M&amp;A A NEW STEP TOWARDS BUSINESS EXPANSION

645
34:45.955 --> 34:46.789
Do we have sound?

646
34:46.856 --> 34:48.457
We do.

647
34:48.524 --> 34:50.359
DAINICHI TV STUDIO

648
34:51.994 --> 34:53.162
Ready.

649
34:54.697 --> 34:56.032
Start.

650
34:57.900 --> 34:59.135
WATER STATION

651
35:01.971 --> 35:04.874
I'm starving. What do you want for lunch?

652
35:04.941 --> 35:06.809
A fried chicken lunch box.

653
35:10.646 --> 35:12.281
How is it?

654
35:13.583 --> 35:15.184
No. I can't hear them at all.

655
35:15.251 --> 35:16.452
No good?

656
35:16.519 --> 35:18.054
This is hard.

657
35:18.120 --> 35:20.489
Hashiguchi, let's change the mic position.

658
35:20.556 --> 35:21.591
Okay.

659
35:22.258 --> 35:24.060
Okay.

660
35:25.361 --> 35:27.263
-Good work. -Good work.

661
35:31.067 --> 35:33.970
THE NEW DESIGN-MIYAMOTO

662
35:39.208 --> 35:41.143
-Huh? -The art staff sent over the set proposal.

663
35:41.210 --> 35:42.111
Oh.

664
35:42.178 --> 35:45.648
HAKONE EKIDEN

665
35:50.052 --> 35:51.187
Where's Miyamoto?

666
35:51.254 --> 35:52.088
In the studio.

667
35:52.655 --> 35:54.223
She's testing the water station.

668
35:54.757 --> 35:55.591
The water station?

669
35:56.158 --> 35:57.727
Toyama wants to broadcast

670
35:57.793 --> 36:00.062
the runners' water station exchanges live during the race.

671
36:00.129 --> 36:02.765
She's testing whether the shotgun mic used

672
36:03.299 --> 36:05.835
for cup sounds in golf coverage

673
36:05.901 --> 36:06.936
might work.

674
36:07.003 --> 36:08.938
I see.

675
36:10.706 --> 36:11.574
Okay.

676
36:14.710 --> 36:16.879
THE OTHER HAKONE EKIDEN INTERVIEW MATERIAL

677
36:18.748 --> 36:22.151
I think it was 2005.

678
36:23.486 --> 36:24.320
Found it.

679
36:24.387 --> 36:25.655
LEG TWO WINNER INTERVIEW MASATO KAI

680
36:26.322 --> 36:27.990
Congrats on the fastest time on the second leg.

681
36:28.057 --> 36:30.359
-Thank you. -That was an incredible run.

682
36:32.194 --> 36:34.463
How did you feel when you crossed the goal first?

683
36:34.530 --> 36:35.498
It's "finish."

684
36:36.899 --> 36:39.168
In track and field, we say "finish," not "goal."

685
36:43.673 --> 36:45.574
I'm sorry.

686
36:49.245 --> 36:51.681
You were asking how I felt when I finished first, right?

687
36:51.747 --> 36:52.615
Yes.

688
36:55.151 --> 36:56.819
DAINICHI TV

689
36:56.886 --> 36:59.722
I guess I was glad I'd believed in them.

690
37:04.193 --> 37:06.095
Coach Moroya taught me that.

691
37:06.162 --> 37:08.964
Trusting your teammates is what matters most.

692
37:10.800 --> 37:12.301
That's why I was able to run.

693
37:14.136 --> 37:15.738
That's it.

694
37:16.272 --> 37:17.273
No.

695
37:17.340 --> 37:19.675
That's not what I mean!

696
37:19.742 --> 37:22.878
Forget it! I'm going over there!

697
37:24.213 --> 37:25.214
-I'll go too. -Yeah.

698
37:25.281 --> 37:26.282
What's going on?

699
37:26.349 --> 37:28.084
They're testing the water station.

700
37:28.150 --> 37:30.152
They're getting nowhere!

701
37:33.422 --> 37:34.690
I'm going too.

702
37:37.760 --> 37:41.030
What about our meeting?

703
37:57.580 --> 37:58.914
Is everyone here?

704
38:00.082 --> 38:01.484
Except Kota.

705
38:04.086 --> 38:05.020
Hayato.

706
38:05.588 --> 38:07.757
Don't forget the most important thing.

707
38:08.324 --> 38:11.160
Our goal of finishing in the top three?

708
38:13.429 --> 38:14.397
Then…

709
38:16.699 --> 38:17.666
Trust.

710
38:19.301 --> 38:20.636
Trust your teammates.

711
38:24.940 --> 38:26.909
Coach Moroya taught me

712
38:27.710 --> 38:29.812
that's what matters most.

713
38:33.883 --> 38:35.584
There's something I want to tell everyone.

714
38:44.160 --> 38:45.795
It's about Kota.

715
38:47.863 --> 38:49.532
I still haven't heard from him.

716
38:51.634 --> 38:55.337
Honestly, I don't know what will happen.

717
38:57.807 --> 38:58.641
But

718
39:00.309 --> 39:01.677
I believe in him.

719
39:03.946 --> 39:07.783
I believe in Kota and everyone who's here now.

720
39:08.651 --> 39:10.019
I want us to pass the sash together.

721
39:12.054 --> 39:13.889
That's what I believe now more than ever.

722
39:17.193 --> 39:18.127
Then

723
39:19.795 --> 39:21.230
how are we

724
39:22.731 --> 39:24.333
supposed to run

725
39:25.801 --> 39:27.837
as one team?

726
39:30.172 --> 39:32.341
There's backlash online.

727
39:32.408 --> 39:35.377
And we all have different feelings about things.

728
39:36.612 --> 39:39.114
But we came together

729
39:40.282 --> 39:44.353
because we want to run.

730
39:49.058 --> 39:50.059
So

731
39:51.327 --> 39:54.063
let's do what we can now

732
39:55.564 --> 39:57.766
and be ready when Kota comes back.

733
39:59.835 --> 40:00.870
-Yes. -Yes.

734
40:02.238 --> 40:03.205
Let's go.

735
40:03.873 --> 40:05.975
-Yes. -Yes.

736
40:20.089 --> 40:22.525
What do you want with the drinks?

737
40:22.591 --> 40:25.694
Gyoza and assorted yakitori.

738
40:29.999 --> 40:33.602
Natsuki, how is it?

739
40:34.870 --> 40:36.639
No. I can barely hear it.

740
40:36.705 --> 40:39.041
WATER STATION ATTENDANT

741
40:39.108 --> 40:40.809
Hashiguchi, let's try running with them.

742
40:40.876 --> 40:41.944
Okay.

743
40:42.511 --> 40:45.681
How many tries is this? I'm almost at my limit.

744
40:46.248 --> 40:47.616
Mr. Matsuzawa,

745
40:48.284 --> 40:50.753
give us something moving this time.

746
40:50.819 --> 40:52.588
Huh? What do you mean?

747
40:53.155 --> 40:57.326
I need some emotional energy or I'm done.

748
40:57.393 --> 40:59.862
Don't put that pressure on me.

749
41:00.429 --> 41:01.463
Okay, here we go.

750
41:04.300 --> 41:05.834
-Mr. Tokushige. -How is it?

751
41:06.502 --> 41:08.470
It's difficult.

752
41:09.438 --> 41:12.041
Of course it won't work from way over there!

753
41:12.541 --> 41:14.810
-Switch with him. -Okay.

754
41:14.877 --> 41:16.512
I will.

755
41:16.579 --> 41:17.546
Thanks.

756
41:18.781 --> 41:21.717
Directionality is everything with this shotgun mic.

757
41:21.784 --> 41:24.753
In this setup, you need to aim it vertically.

758
41:25.354 --> 41:27.156
Okay, go ahead!

759
41:27.222 --> 41:29.992
Okay, Miyamoto! Try it!

760
41:31.794 --> 41:33.729
All right, here we go.

761
41:34.997 --> 41:35.998
Ready.

762
41:39.368 --> 41:40.369
Start!

763
41:41.136 --> 41:43.739
WATER STATION

764
41:52.815 --> 41:53.882
No good?

765
41:54.683 --> 41:55.918
Toyama!

766
41:57.086 --> 41:58.821
We're all fighting together!

767
41:59.855 --> 42:00.756
Huh?

768
42:01.557 --> 42:05.661
So you're not alone!

769
42:08.197 --> 42:10.566
We got it! We recorded it!

770
42:10.633 --> 42:12.401
You did it!

771
42:14.336 --> 42:15.404
How was it?

772
42:15.471 --> 42:19.074
Toyama! We're all fighting together!

773
42:22.945 --> 42:24.613
So you're not alone!

774
42:26.015 --> 42:28.350
-Yeah! -Yeah!

775
42:28.417 --> 42:30.285
-Thank you! -Oh!

776
42:30.352 --> 42:31.920
Natsuki!

777
42:31.987 --> 42:34.523
Never give up!

778
42:35.391 --> 42:38.027
Matsuzawa, that was pretty good. It actually moved me.

779
42:39.595 --> 42:43.165
Actually, Mr. Tokushige said that to me a long time ago.

780
42:43.232 --> 42:44.433
Really?

781
42:44.500 --> 42:47.670
He probably doesn't even remember.

782
42:48.270 --> 42:50.272
That actually got to me too.

783
42:50.339 --> 42:51.240
Huh?

784
42:53.809 --> 42:55.044
Never…

785
42:55.110 --> 42:56.812
He can say some good things.

786
42:58.080 --> 43:00.749
HAKONE EKIDEN

787
43:04.953 --> 43:05.954
Thank you.

788
43:08.057 --> 43:12.327
I assumed it was normal that we couldn't pick up the runners' voices.

789
43:13.095 --> 43:15.030
I never even thought about trying.

790
43:17.099 --> 43:18.300
Somewhere along the way,

791
43:18.367 --> 43:20.703
I guess I got used to it.

792
43:22.504 --> 43:24.306
Toyama and the others

793
43:24.373 --> 43:25.974
reminded me to go back to basics.

794
43:28.077 --> 43:30.312
-Me too. -Huh?

795
43:30.879 --> 43:32.214
That's right.

796
43:33.582 --> 43:36.051
If you have something you believe in, that's enough.

797
43:39.922 --> 43:42.091
Let's go with the first design.

798
43:43.325 --> 43:44.259
Okay.

799
44:01.477 --> 44:03.512
33 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

800
44:03.579 --> 44:05.581
One month to go.

801
44:08.383 --> 44:10.018
Let's do Hakone our way.

802
44:11.520 --> 44:12.554
Yes.

803
44:18.727 --> 44:19.895
GENERAL PRODUCTION BUREAU

804
44:19.962 --> 44:21.997
GENERAL PRODUCTION BUREAU BUREAU CHIEF-TAKESHI KUROISHI

805
44:26.001 --> 44:27.736
CHIEF PRODUCER GROUP: TOKUSHIGE, TSUCHIYA, TACHIBANA, NISHIKAWA, YAMANO

806
44:31.173 --> 44:32.207
‎NEXT ORETACHINO HAKONEEKIDEN

807
44:53.195 --> 44:54.830
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP COLLEGE EKIDEN RACE

808
45:00.202 --> 45:02.004
I might not be able to pass the sash.

809
45:02.070 --> 45:02.905
33 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

810
45:02.971 --> 45:04.006
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION UNRELATED TO REAL PEOPLE OR GROUPS.
